+- RULE: The production evidence gate now requires at least 1000 samples (10× the original 100-cycle minimum), the existing fixed 10-sample allocator warmup, a 500-sample trailing half-run with no footprint increase, and total post-warmup growth no greater than `256 KiB` (1% of the upper 25 MiB provisional envelope). Raw evidence records every parameter, transition count, jump cycle, ownership counter, and sample. Positive high-water convergence plus late-rise and oversized-high-water negative tests bind the classifier; the original rise-plus-plateau negative remains.
