+- INVESTIGATION: A bounded process-local 1000-cycle SwiftPM/loopback run captured every physical-footprint jump and 100-cycle segment. Jumps ended at cycle 491; segments 501–600 through 901–1000 each changed by `0 B`. After the fixed 10-sample warmup, net growth was `229,400 B`; descriptors stayed `3`, threads stayed `9`, and every post-cleanup HEV session, read, and queue count was zero. Boundary start/stop and HEV start/main-return counters were exactly one per cycle. A preceding 500-cycle repeat still had two trailing jumps, proving 500 cycles were insufficient.
+- RULE: The production evidence gate now requires at least 1000 samples (10× the original 100-cycle minimum), the existing fixed 10-sample allocator warmup, a 500-sample trailing half-run with no footprint increase, and total post-warmup growth no greater than `256 KiB` (1% of the upper 25 MiB provisional envelope). Raw evidence records every parameter, transition count, jump cycle, ownership counter, and sample. Positive high-water convergence plus late-rise and oversized-high-water negative tests bind the classifier; the original rise-plus-plateau negative remains.
+- ANOMALY/FIX: The first extended attempt stopped at cycle 257 with Swift signal 5 because the test payload used checked `UInt8(iteration)`. `UInt8(truncatingIfNeeded:)` removes that artificial 255-cycle harness limit while address and port continue to identify each flow. The 1000-cycle investigation passed in 41.00 seconds. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.
+
